{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nNow I have the full picture. Let me analyze the bug and implement the fix.\n\n**The Bug:** `_normalize_requested_path` calls `unquote()` only once. Double-encoded paths like `%252e%252e%252fsecrets.csv` decode to `%2e%2e%2fsecrets.csv` after one pass — the `..` substring check doesn't catch it. Additionally, Windows drive-letter paths like `C:\\temp\\secrets.csv` bypass all checks on Linux.\n\n**The Fix:** Repeatedly unquote until stable, and block drive-letter absolute paths.\n\n"}}
